        <section id="sect-00003">
          <title>[H2]Mass</title>
          <para id="para-00007">Although we don't make the distinction very carefully in everyday life on Earth, strictly speaking the kilogram is a unit of mass (measuring the quantity of matter in a body, roughly how many atoms it has) while the pound is a unit of weight (measuring how strongly Earth's gravity pulls on a body).</para>
          <para id="para-00008">The most commonly used quantities of mass of the metric system are the following.
